From 9f97925f3caee6c51bf821f2139863cd8f4c5ca0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HazzPika <188178761+HazzPika@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:26:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] airoha: en7528: add FiberHome SR1041Y

GPON ONT + router TM supplies with Unifi in Malaysia: EN7561DU (EN7528
platform, "free bootbase"), 256 MB, 256 MiB Micron MT29F2G01 SPI-NAND,
4x GbE, MT7915 DBDC on PCIe, EN7571 xPON with an EN7570 laser driver.

- runs from bank B in the stock bank format: kernel trx in UBI volume
  ID 0 (what the bootbase loads), rootfs and rootfs_data alongside;
  bank A keeps the stock firmware; KernelB attached as linux,ubi
- sysupgrade into bank B, kernel volume created static with ID 0;
  alphawrt-bootbank with the GN630V interface, flipping the boot flag
  record the bootbase reads from bank A's UBI volumes 3/4
- MACs and MT7915 calibration from the stock UBIFS "factory" volume on
  the "config" UBI, attached read-only; mounted in 09_mount_factory_data
  through that UBI device ("ubi:NAME" only searches ubi0)
- MT7915 on the main PCIe link only: binding through HIF2 (pcie0)
  resets the SoC
- GbE PHYs enabled (the dtsi disables them); UART clock 7.3728 MHz, as
  the free bootbase leaves the XYD divider set up
- no GPON yet: xpon, gdm2 and the EN7571 are left disabled

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
